# Checked by `crates/spacelab/tests/release_metadata.rs`, which reads this file and the workspace
# manifest and fails if `version`, `license`, `repository-code` or `title` disagree with them. A
# citation file that quietly outlives the release it names is the same defect class as a
# hand-maintained crate table, and it is fixed the same way: nothing here is a transcription that
# nothing checks.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: spacelab
abstract: >-
  Astrodynamics in Rust, organised around independent verification: fundamental astronomy and
  reference frames, SGP4, numerical and semi-analytical propagation with the full IERS 2010 force
  stack, orbit determination, GNSS, satellite laser ranging, closed-loop control, coverage and
  constellation design, and Earth-observation geometry. Every published number is checked against a
  lineage that did not come from the project, and each check is recorded with its oracle and its
  residual in docs/verification.md.
authors:
  - family-names: Gradina
    given-names: Ilia
    email: ilia.gradina@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/SpaceDataLab/spacelab"
license:
  - MIT
  - Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
keywords:
  - astrodynamics
  - orbit-determination
  - orbital-mechanics
  - SGP4
  - GNSS
  - satellite-laser-ranging
  - reference-frames
  - IERS
  - rust
